.\" Man page for amf (almanac-model-fetch).
.\" Kept in the packaging directory rather than generated at build time, so
.\" that building the RPM needs no extra crates. If the CLI changes, this
.\" changes with it.
.TH AMF 1 "2026-08-09" "almanac-model-fetch 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amf \- fetch, verify, and bundle AI models for airgapped import
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amf fetch
.I REPO_SPEC\fR...
.BR \-\-usb " " \fIPATH\fR
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B amf verify
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-public\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-upstream\-key
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B amf list
.I PATH
.br
.B amf keygen
.RB [ \-\-secret
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-public
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B amf trust
.I SUBCOMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amf
runs on a networked machine. It downloads a model you choose, verifies it
against upstream\-published hashes as it streams, captures what provenance
exists, signs the result, and writes a self\-contained bundle that a USB drive
can carry to an airgapped machine with no network at all.
.PP
A revision always resolves to an immutable commit SHA before anything is
fetched, and the bundle records that SHA rather than the branch name. If a host
cannot name its head commit in full, the bundle records the abbreviated id
.I as
abbreviated and says so \(em it never presents a prefix as an immutable
revision.
.SH REPO SPECS
Repository specs are
.IR org/name [ @revision ][ :variant ].
Omitting the variant gives an interactive picker; pass
.B \-\-variant
for scripts, or
.B \-\-yes
to take the default without prompting.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS fetch
Fetch one or more models onto a drive. Each spec is bundled separately.
.TP
.BI \-\-usb " PATH"
Destination drive or directory. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-variant " NAME"
Quantisation to fetch, when the spec does not name one.
.TP
.BI \-\-source " HOST"
Source host, either
.B hf
(default) or
.BR modelscope .
ModelScope is for operators who cannot reach HuggingFace; the tool never falls
back to it automatically, because switching hosts changes what the bundle can
prove.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Accept the default variant without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Proceed past warnings. Does not override the refusal to write to a FAT
filesystem.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Refuse to write a bundle unless the upstream commit signature verified.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-corroborate
Skip cross\-checking the file hash against the other host.
.TP
.BI \-\-corroborate\-with " HOST:REPO"
Corroborate against a specific repository, for mirrors that are not named
identically upstream.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-corroboration
Refuse to write a bundle unless the other host confirms the hashes.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Secret key used to sign the bundle manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-trust\-store " PATH"
Trust store location. Must match the store
.B amf trust
was pointed at, or pinned keys will not be found.
.SS verify
Re\-verify a bundle, or every bundle on a drive. This is the airgapped\-side
command: it needs no network, no keyserver, and no correct clock.
.TP
.BI \-\-public\-key " PATH"
Public key to check the bundle signature against.
.TP
.BI \-\-upstream\-key " PATH"
Armored PGP public key to check the captured upstream commit signature against,
obtained out of band.
.SS list
Inventory the bundles on a drive or directory.
.SS keygen
Generate the fetcher's signing keypair. The public half goes to the airgapped
machine.
.TP
.BI \-\-secret " PATH"
Where to write the secret key. Default
.BR amf.key .
.TP
.BI \-\-public " PATH"
Where to write the public key. Default
.BR amf.pub .
.TP
.BI \-\-comment " TEXT"
Comment identifying this fetcher.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " TEXT"
Password\-protect the secret key.
.SS trust
Manage pinned upstream signing keys and observed\-fingerprint history.
.TP
.B trust list
Show pinned keys and every fingerprint ever observed.
.TP
.BI "trust add " "HOST KEY_FILE"
Pin a host's public key, which enables real Tier\-2 verification for it.
.TP
.BI "trust remove " HOST
Remove a host's pinned key.
.SH CROSS-SOURCE CORROBORATION
Every fetch asks the other host whether it publishes the same SHA\-256 before
downloading anything. A miss is silent \(em an operator who chose ModelScope
because HuggingFace is blocked cannot be expected to reach it. A disagreement
is loud and is recorded in the manifest, but does not by itself abort: two
hosts can legitimately differ after a re\-quantisation, unlike a single host
contradicting its own signed tree, which always aborts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/almanac\-model\-fetch/trust.json
Default trust store: pinned upstream keys and observed\-fingerprint history.
Overridden by
.B \-\-trust\-store
or
.BR $AMF_TRUST_STORE .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMF_TRUST_STORE
Path to the trust store, overriding the default location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; the reason is printed to standard error. Verification
failures are reported this way, not as a partial success.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create the signing key once, then fetch a model onto a drive:
.PP
.nf
.RS
amf keygen \-\-secret amf.key \-\-public amf.pub
amf fetch unsloth/Llama\-3.2\-1B\-Instruct\-GGUF:Q4_K_M \\
    \-\-usb /mnt/usb \-\-key amf.key
.RE
.fi
.PP
On the airgapped machine, with no network:
.PP
.nf
.RS
amf verify /mnt/usb \-\-public\-key amf.pub
amf list /mnt/usb
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The design and trust model are documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/almanac\-model\-fetch/ARCHITECTURE.md
.SH AUTHOR
https://github.com/clemperorpenguin/almanac\-model\-fetch
